From 2d025c68c25a0dc722660dec2dbf132a7e6c5301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:29:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card and the /btw card speak pt-BR

Zeo's own cards in the agent thread read their text through zeo_i18n's t!
from locales/<language>/agent-ui.ftl, in en-US and pt-BR: the tasks card
(0037 and the many patches since) -- its header, pill, row controls and
their aria labels, the stop prompt, the details, the status, the sub-thread
rows -- and the /btw side-question card (0115). The en-US file is the code's
English byte for byte. The pill's four cases are one message selecting on
both counts; the tool count's plural is the message's.

Only surfaces that are wholly Zeo's are translated. The question card
(elicitation) and the subagent card are Zed's with Zeo additions, the tool
cards' menu sits in Zed's agent menu and the BTW button in Zed's queue: they
stay English until Zed translates its part, so no screen mixes the two.
"Waiting for you" stays English too: the Agent Tasks panel and Zed's subagent
card share it.

At the end of the claude-agent-acp-plus group, after 0176: the cards are that
group's, and ai-jail (whose 0179 also needs agent_ui's dependency) requires it.
---

